# Vulnerability inherited from the QuBins base image
# (ghcr.io/qubins/images:latest-small). racetraQ layers only its own
# app on top and adds no new vulnerable code. pyo3's out-of-bounds read
# in nth/nth_back (pulled via rattler and rpds in the base) is not
# reachable in racetraQ's usage. Fixed in pyo3 0.29.0; the base image
# has not yet rebased. Justified upstream in the QuBins .trivyignore.
GHSA-36hh-v3qg-5jq4

# Trivy layer-resolution artefacts in the QuBins base image, not packages
# racetraQ ships:
#   GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964  msgpack     reported 1.1.2  (image has 1.2.3)
#   CVE-2025-47273       setuptools  reported 70.3.0 (image has 84.0.0)
#   CVE-2026-97687/97689 urllib3     reported 2.7.0  (image has 2.8.0)
# Trivy reads them from a base layer whose files a later base layer
# replaces; the image has a single site-packages tree with the fixed
# versions (the Dockerfile floors all three again). QuBins verified this
# and suppresses the same IDs in its own .trivyignore
# (github.com/QuBins/qiskit-images, "Trivy layer-resolution artefacts"),
# but a repo-level ignore file does not travel with the image, so an image
# built on top needs its own. Drop these when the base stops carrying the
# superseded layers or Trivy resolves overwritten metadata across layers.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
